  "footnotes": [
   "Note:—The Middle section comprises the 17 prefectures of Tokyo, Kanagawa, Saitama, Chiba, Ibaragi, Tochigi, Gumma, Nagano, Yamanashi, Shizuoka, Aichi, Miye, Gifu, Shiga, Fukui, Ishikawa, Toyama; the Northern section comprises the 7 prefectures of Niigata, Fukushima, Miyagi, Yamagata, Akita, Iwate Aomori; the Western section consists of Kyoto, Ōsaka, Nara, Wakayama, Hyogo, Okayama, Hiroshima, Yamaguchi, Shimane, Tottori; Shikoku comprises Tokushima, Kagawa, Ehime and Kōchi; Kyūshu comprises Nagasaki, Saga, Fukuoka, Kumamoto, Ōita, Miyazaki, Kagoshima, and Okinawa; Hokkaidō covers all the districts under its jurisdiction. This classification holds good for all the tables to be given hereafter."
